selection_rule:
20 cells, drawn in this order, each group excluding cells already drawn:
(a) misprint log, 5: every logged cell that a computed path reads (the four that the
    two-row sensitivity uses), and 1 more drawn from the other logged cells;
(b) the one cell on which the two entries disagreed, 1;
(c) doubtful, 4: cells whose entry note gives an alternative reading or a damaged figure
    ("possibly", "as best read", blotted, broken, malformed, damaged), drawn at random;
(d) the 1780 neighbours, 5: cells the table path reads at Adams's places of 1769, 1771,
    1783 and 1786 (from which the 1780 place is interpolated), one per place and one more
    from their union, drawn at random;
(e) random, 5: drawn from all remaining route-B cells.
Logged misprint cells outside the 1,855 (Table XIII row 720 is a step-3d cell) are not
eligible. There are more forced cells than places, so groups (a) to (d) are themselves
sampled; the rule and the seed were fixed before the draw.
